      "message": "It looks like a 64KiB block size being enforced by `LENGTH \u003d (((192 * 1024) / 0x10000) * 0x10000)`, which explains why 192KiB is the smallest workable size.\n\nFrom prepossessed linker script:\n\n```ld\nMEMORY\n{\n FLASH (rx) : ORIGIN \u003d (0x10058000 + (0)), LENGTH \u003d (((192 * 1024) / 0x10000) * 0x10000)\n IRAM (rw) : ORIGIN \u003d (0x200C0000 - (((181 * 1024) + (4 * 1024)) - (96 * 1024))), LENGTH \u003d (((181 * 1024) + (4 * 1024)) - (4 * 1024))\n CDRAM (rx) : ORIGIN \u003d 0x10058000 + (0), LENGTH \u003d (((192 * 1024) / 0x10000) * 0x10000)\n}\n```",
